# Blockchain Protocol
bc:BC-9980 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bc:DistributedSystemProtocol ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bc:ConsensusAlgorithm ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bc:PeertoPeerProtocol ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bc:CryptographicProtocol ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bc:NetworkProtocol ;
    rdfs:subClassOf bc:StateMachineReplication ;
    rdfs:label "Blockchain Protocol"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Foundational rule set governing distributed ledger system operation comprising consensus mechanisms (algorithmic procedures enabling network-wide agreement on canonical state without centralized authority including Proof of Work PoW SHA-256 hash puzzles requiring computational expenditure Bitcoin 10-minute target block time difficulty adjustment every 2,016 blocks maintaining probabilistic finality 6-confirmation standard 99.9% security, Proof of Stake PoS validator selection weighted by token stake Ethereum Beacon Chain 32 ETH minimum deposit Casper FFG finality gadget achieving economic finality through slashing 1-4 ETH penalties equivocation offline infractions, Byzantine Fault Tolerance BFT Practical Byzantine Fault Tolerance PBFT tolerating f < n/3 faulty nodes deterministic finality single-slot confirmation Tendermint Core 67% supermajority voting rounds, Delegated Proof of Stake DPoS witness election systems EOS 21 block producers 0.5-second block time, Nominated Proof of Stake NPoS Polkadot validator nomination 297 active validators 24-hour era rotation), network communication protocols (peer-to-peer topology gossip protocols epidemic information dissemination Bitcoin INV/GETDATA messages Ethereum devp2p RLPx encryption authenticated transport Kademlia DHT distributed hash tables peer discovery 8-125 peer connections NAT traversal UPnP/STUN/TURN, block propagation mechanisms Bitcoin compact blocks 99% bandwidth reduction BIP-152 high-bandwidth relay mode <1s propagation to 90% network Ethereum Firehose 6-second slot times attestation aggregation, transaction mempool management fee market priority queuing Bitcoin replace-by-fee RBF transaction replacement Ethereum EIP-1559 base fee BASEFEE + priority tip dynamic block space pricing 50% burn mechanism), transaction validation rules (cryptographic signature verification ECDSA secp256k1 256-bit private keys elliptic curve digital signatures Ed25519 Schnorr signatures BIP-340 batch verification Ethereum EIP-2930 access lists gas optimization, double-spend prevention UTXO unspent transaction output model Bitcoin preventing same output multiple spends account-based nonce sequencing Ethereum incrementing transaction counters, state transition validation deterministic virtual machine execution Ethereum Virtual Machine EVM 256-bit word size stack-based architecture gas metering computational cost pricing preventing denial-of-service attacks, smart contract validation Solidity bytecode compilation ABI application binary interface function selectors 4-byte signatures, Merkle proof verification SPV simplified payment verification light clients validating transactions without full blockchain download 80-byte block headers Merkle path proofs logarithmic verification complexity O(log n)), state management approaches (UTXO model Bitcoin stateless design each transaction referencing prior outputs no global account state parallelizable validation privacy advantages coin mixing, account model Ethereum global state trie accounts storing balances nonce code storage Patricia Merkle Tree 32-byte Keccak-256 hashes 16^64 address space, state trie structures world state accounts contract storage receipt tries Merkle Patricia Tries prefix compression pruning nodes, state synchronization snapshots fast sync Ethereum Geth warp sync Parity downloading recent state checkpoints without replaying entire history reducing sync time weeks → hours), security guarantees (51% attack resistance hash rate distribution Bitcoin 120 EH/s January 2025 requiring $10B+ capital expenditure 51% majority attack economic infeasibility Ethereum 32M ETH staked $110B at $3,400/ETH slashing penalties, finality properties probabilistic finality PoW 6-confirmation standard 99.9% reversion probability < 0.1% absolute finality BFT Tendermint instant finality upon block commit economic finality PoS Ethereum finalized epochs irreversible without mass validator slashing, cryptoeconomic security slashing conditions double-signing attestations proposing conflicting blocks penalties 1 ETH minimum 4 ETH maximum validator balance reduction ejection from validator set, Sybil resistance mechanisms work-based PoW computational expenditure stake-based PoS capital lockup opportunity cost 4-10% staking yields identity-based permissioned networks certificate authorities consortium membership, network partition tolerance CAP theorem consistency availability partition tolerance trade-offs eventual consistency Bitcoin accepting temporary forks canonical chain reorganization longest chain rule strong consistency Tendermint BFT halting progress under 33% Byzantine failures), interoperability standards (cross-chain communication protocols Cosmos IBC Inter-Blockchain Communication relayer infrastructure light client verification 50+ IBC-enabled chains January 2025 Osmosis Terra Juno Akash Evmos, bridge mechanisms token wrapping WBTC Wrapped Bitcoin $8.2B TVL January 2025 custodial bridges centralized validators decentralized bridges multi-signature thresholds Ethereum Layer-2 rollups optimistic rollups Optimism Arbitrum fraud proofs 7-day challenge periods zero-knowledge rollups zkSync StarkNet validity proofs SNARK/STARK cryptographic verification, atomic swaps hash time-locked contracts HTLC Bitcoin Lightning Network payment channels conditional execution time-locked refunds cross-chain asset exchange), protocol governance mechanisms (on-chain governance token-weighted voting Polkadot OpenGov public referenda conviction voting time-weighted preferences treasury allocation parachain slot auctions, off-chain governance improvement proposal processes Bitcoin BIP Bitcoin Improvement Proposal community consensus miner signaling soft forks backward compatibility hard forks network-wide upgrades Ethereum EIP Ethereum Improvement Proposal EIP-1559 fee market reform EIP-4844 proto-danksharding blob transactions, stakeholder coordination miners validators node operators developers users economic ince